 .. versionadded:: 3.0
 
-Default: ``None``
+Default: ``'strict-origin'``
+
+If set to ``None``, the :class:`~django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware`
+will not set the :ref:`referrer-policy` header.
+
+.. _referrer-policy:
+
+The ``Referrer-Policy`` HTTP header lets a site specify a Referrer-Policy
+that applies to all navigations within the site's context. The policy can
+be one of the following values:
+
+``no-referrer``
+    The browser will never send the ``Referer`` header to any origin.
+
+``no-referrer-when-downgrade``
+    Full URL is sent as ``Referer`` header when performing a same-origin
+    request, but only the origin of the URL is sent when performing a
+    cross-origin request (e.g. when navigating from ``https://example.org/``
+    to ``https://example.com/``).
+
+``origin``
+    Only the origin of the URL is sent when performing a same-origin request
+    or a cross-origin request.
+
+``origin-when-cross-origin``
+    Full URL is sent when performing a same-origin request, but only the
+    origin is sent for cross-origin requests.
+
+``same-origin``
+    Full URL is sent only when performing a same-origin request. For
+    cross-origin requests, the header is not sent.
+
+``strict-origin``
+    Only the origin is sent when performing a same-origin request. For
+    cross-origin requests, the header is not sent.
+
+``strict-origin-when-cross-origin``
+    Full URL is sent when performing a same-origin request, but only the
+    origin is sent for cross-origin requests. For cross-origin requests
+    that are HTTP requests (as opposed to HTTPS), the header is not sent.
 
